WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
- There's an alchemy to recognition,

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.960
when you see yourself and it,

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.100
something happens,
something chemical happens.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.520
It's a little bit like magic.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.120
It's a validation of like, I exist.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.703
(gentle music)

00:00:20.118 --> 00:00:22.580
- White people get to be
well rounded in the media,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.370
they get to be everything.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.870
They get to be everyone and everything.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.000
What about the rest of us?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.210
We just have to be maids,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.890
or we just have to be servants.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.670
We have to be slaves, we
have to be serving you.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.620
- So, I graduated from Boston University,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.220
I went to Oxford to study Shakespeare,

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.300
and then I got to Chicago.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.290
I moved to Chicago and I was like,

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.470
I'm going to be an actor now.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.620
And all the roles I was getting,

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.530
were named Maria first of all,

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.737
and most of the things
I had to say are like

00:00:49.737 --> 00:00:51.210
"Yes Mr. Jones, through here".

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.090
Like that's all they wanted from me.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.130
- The interesting thing about the way

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.270
an entire group of people

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.510
are portrayed in film and television,

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.020
is that people tend to believe that.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:05.763
Subconsciously that tells me
where my place in life is.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.880
- People have gotten away with not knowing

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.250
how to work with people of color

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.050
because they've never really had to.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.720
With the beauty industry,
- Yeah.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.330
- For them not to typecast us

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:19.350
as being the class of women
that are afraid to wear color.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.530
- Oh no, no, no, no.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.910
Like all of this color's invented.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.430
Like you can't tell me I can't have it.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.070
And also I will not be trained to believe

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.640
that I'm not worthy of it.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.320
- The perception is that
one color works for all.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.660
Black has different shades.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.530
- There's 27 countries that
make up the Latin diaspora.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:35.980
We're not one thing.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.750
Sometimes they brownface me too much,

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.480
or like orange me, or they wipe me out.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.240
- I hate when people
start contouring my nose

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.290
and I didn't ask for it.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.070
Like why is my face not
good enough for you?

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:45.970
This is just my face.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.870
- Good, but just as pretty.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:48.756
I like this.

00:01:48.756 --> 00:01:50.470
I love this palette.
- I love it.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:51.490
Looking gorgeous.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.261
(laughter)

00:01:54.261 --> 00:01:55.830
- It was great. (laughter)

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.790
You're starting to see
more people of color

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.670
as directors, as EPs, grips,

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.410
screenwriters, makeup artists

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.850
and I think that we are coming along.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.350
But I do think that we
have a very long way to go.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.670
- I feel things changing

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.230
and I'm grateful for that change.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.190
As a black woman,

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.910
there're a lot more
voices in the industry,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.250
that sound like mine.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.990
That feel true and honest,

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.970
to not just me, but to
my mother and my aunts

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.923
and the community that raised me.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.220
- I'm creating a Latina show,

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.220
where Latinas are at the
center and the forefront.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.413
I wanted it to look like we look.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.150
- You can be beautiful with
whatever feature that you have.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.040
Tall, dark, wide nose, big lips.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.610
Plus size, petite.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.470
Makeup should be used as tool,

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.963
as a tool to enhance.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.920
- When my makeup is done correctly,

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.060
I feel like I'm being
valued as and artist.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.268
And then the character is
being valued as a human.

00:02:56.268 --> 00:02:58.851
(gentle music)

